          "description": "Source block 7: தம்பி!..என் கோகிலாவைத் தீ விழுங்கிட்டுது!..இல்ல! அந்தத் தீயவன் ஜம்புலிங்க பூபதி விழுங்கிட்டான்! எந்தப் பெண்ணுக்காக இதுவரையில் உயிர் வாழ்ந்தே"
        },
        "speaker_label": null,
        "speaker_label_origin": "source-unlabelled",
        "source_delimiter": null,
        "page_provenance": [
          {
            "pdf_page": 84,
            "printed_page": 83
          }
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "mode": "prose-faithful",
        "notes": [
          "The source prints no speaker label for this spoken unit; no speaker or immutable dialogue ID is inferred."
        ],
        "english_text": "Brother!.. Fire has swallowed my Kokila!.. No! That evil man Jambuling Bhoopathi swallowed her! The girl for whose sake I lived all these years; the girl whose life I wanted to blossom and spread fragrance.... for whose sake I kept the mysteries of this estate palace hidden; the girl for whose sake I wandered like a living corpse without even saying who I was—now that very girl is gone, what is left for me? Who is Jambuling Bhoopathi, whom this whole town thinks is a noble man?... A drunkard!.... A murderer!... A robber!... A scoundrel!... A lust-crazed man!... A human beast who treats a crowd of maidens as merchandise!... This Maragatham was made the bedchamber doll of that human beast! Kokila is the child born to the two of us!... Now that you are gone, what do I have left? This very moment I am leaving for his private palace! There is a Goddess statue there in what is called the temple; turn it and inside is that criminal’s pleasure chamber! He ruined the lives of so many young women; he ordered even the huts where the poor live to be set on fire and planned to burn us alive. I will take revenge for revenge!..."
      }
